Write a program to input the electricity unit consumed and calculate the total electricity bill according to the given conditions:

For the first 50 units Rs. 3.50/unit

For the next 100 units Rs. 4.50/unit

For the next 100 units Rs. 5.20/unit

For units above 250 Rs. 6.75/unit

An additional surcharge of 20% is added to the bill.

Input format:

An integer representing total units consumed.

Output format :

A float value representing the total electricity bill in rupees.

Refer to the sample output for formatting specifications.

Code constraints:

0 units <= 100000

Sample test cases:

Input 1:

50

Output 1:

210.00




import java.util.Scanner;
class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int unit = sc.nextInt();
        double amount=0.0;
        if(unit>=0 && unit<=50){
            amount=unit*3.50;
        }else if(unit>=50 && unit<=150){
            amount=(175)+(unit-50)*4.50;
        }else if(unit>=150 && unit<=250){
            amount=(175)+(450)+(unit-150)*5.20;
        }else if(unit>250){
            amount=(175)+(450)+(520)+(unit-250)*6.75;
        }
        System.out.printf("%.2f",amount+(amount*0.20));
    }
}
